James sought clarification on a statement regarding how damages are modeled in relation to temperature, specifically mentioning that "Damages are often modeled as being convex in temperature: each additional degree of warming is worse." He felt this didn't adequately convey the concept of convexity. In response, I rephrased the statement to enhance its clarity: “Damages are often modeled as convex in temperature: each additional degree of warming causes greater harm than the degree before it, so damages accelerate as temperatures rise.” This revision emphasized the accelerating nature of damages with increasing temperatures.
